 "conclusion": {
  "consequence": "more exposures cannot fix this. The composition operator rejects the second witness before looking at it, so the 'see it twice, then generalize' fallback is closed too. The next mechanism must abstract over the Semantic IR with typed holes and no arity equality, which is what \u00a79.2 specifies and what the current lift does not do.",
  "design_it_kills": "Move 3 / \u00a79.4.3 'algebraic skill composition' is not buildable on the current generalizer; wiring more engines into UnifiedModel will not change this, and claiming otherwise would be the accumulation-the-thesis-warns-about.",
  "instant_learning_claim_as_implemented": "FALSE",
  "why": "lift_python_subtree_morphism returns a statement-slice copy of the one fix (observed arities 10, 1, 0 for three real click/werkzeug fixes). It is therefore not a rule: 0 of 6 cross-commit applications unified, including within the same project (a click skill on a click bug), and 0 of 3 pairs anti-unified, every refusal being ARITY_MISMATCH_BEFORE from the operator's own equality precondition."
 },
